title: 'Ryan Singer, Shape Up, chapter "Set Boundaries" (Basecamp): an appetite is a budget fixed before the design, and scope bends to fit it.'
pid: 3c5d2409-9fdd-4360-a63b-c59fdd6ef686
body: |2-
  https://basecamp.com/shapeup/1.2-chapter-03
  "An appetite is completely different from an estimate": an estimate
  starts with a design and ends with a number; an appetite starts
  with a number and ends with a design. Ask "what's really going
  wrong?" before "what could we build?"; one six-week request became a
  one-day fix. A request with no edges is "a grab-bag, not a
  project". This is the question Jeff gave Tay: how far should this go.
